            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for the web, then the Telugu for a phone charger."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: అసౌకర్యం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అసౌకర్యం — asaukaryaṁ — \"inconvenience\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆలస్యం వల్ల కలిగిన అసౌకర్యానికి క్షమించండి. ālasyaṁ valla kaligina asaukaryāniki kṣamiñcaṇḍi. We are sorry for the inconvenience caused by the delay."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అ-, not, + సౌకర్యం, comfort. Station announcements use this sentence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అసౌకర్యం (asaukaryaṁ) is built from Sanskrit a-, \"not\", and saukarya, \"ease, practicability\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
