          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఇబ్బంది — ibbandi — \"trouble; difficulty\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కొత్త నగరంలో భాష వల్ల ఇబ్బంది పడ్డాం. kotta nagaraṁlō bhāṣa valla ibbandi paḍḍāṁ. In the new city we had trouble because of the language."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఇబ్బంది (ibbandi) పడు, to have trouble; ఇబ్బంది (ibbandi) పెట్టు, to cause someone trouble."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఇబ్బంది (ibbandi) is native Dravidian: DEDR 524 lists Telugu ibbandi, \"difficulty, inconvenience\", beside iṟuku, \"to be squeezed, to be stuck in\", and ikkaṭṭu, \"hardship\". A tight spot became a difficulty."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
